<!--
  pfSense filterlog without a hostname: this FreeBSD syslogd (14.0-CURRENT,
  tested on pfsense.lab) sends "<PRI>Mmm dd hh:mm:ss filterlog[pid]: <csv>"
  — no hostname between the timestamp and the tag, unlike the native
  decoder's example (0455-pfsense_decoders.xml, which expects
  "... pfSense filterlog: ...").

  Wazuh's syslog pre-decoder then assigns the token "filterlog[pid]:" to
  the hostname field, leaving program_name empty: the native "pf" decoder
  (matched on <program_name>filterlog</program_name>) never matches,
  silently (wazuh-logtest confirms: "No decoder matched").

  Fallback decoder, matched on <prematch> (raw text) rather than
  program_name. Named differently ("pf-nohost") to coexist with the native
  decoder without conflict — each covers a different source format.

  Gotchas hit while building it (Wazuh offsets, not standard regex):
  - `\[` followed by a `[0-9]` class broke Wazuh's XML/regex parser at
    validation time ("Syntax error on regex") — literal `\[\d+\]` passes,
    `\[[0-9]+\]` does not. Stick to `\d`, never a class right next to an
    escaped bracket.
  - `offset="after_prematch"` only exists when prematch and regex are in
    the SAME <decoder> (cf. native "agent-buffer" in
    0005-wazuh_decoders.xml) — invalid between a decoder and its
    <parent>. Between decoders, only `after_parent` (after the parent's
    match, whatever it is) and `after_regex` (after the parent's <regex>)
    are valid.
  - A decoder can only be a <parent> if it is directly at the top level:
    no grandchild (parent of a parent). Multi-field continuation is done
    by repeating the SAME decoder name several times with <parent> all
    pointing back to the root — exactly the pattern the native pf-fields
    ×3 uses. Breaking this pattern (parenting a child on another child, or
    renaming each step) fails the load ("Invalid offset value:
    '<decoder name>'").
-->
<decoder name="pf-nohost">
  <prematch>filterlog[\d+]: </prematch>
</decoder>

<decoder name="pf-nohost-fields">
  <parent>pf-nohost</parent>
  <regex offset="after_parent">^\S*,\S*,\S*,(\S*),\S*,\S*,(\S*),</regex>
  <order>id,action</order>
</decoder>

<decoder name="pf-nohost-fields">
  <parent>pf-nohost</parent>
  <regex offset="after_regex">\S*,\S*,\S*,\S*,\S*,\S*,\S*,\S*,\S*,(\S*),\S*,(\S*),(\S*),</regex>
  <order>protocol,srcip,dstip</order>
</decoder>

<decoder name="pf-nohost-fields">
  <parent>pf-nohost</parent>
  <regex offset="after_regex">(\d*),(\d*),\S*</regex>
  <order>srcport,dstport</order>
</decoder>
